prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: one clean reference-art contact sheet for a developer collaboration board, for subsequent manual vector adaptation. This is NOT a UI screenshot, production icon atlas or app proof.

Create one coherent restrained retro-cartoon family: functional control glyphs, all ten ticket-state silhouettes, and distinct compact bot-role illustrations. Quiet readable hierarchy like a warm cream collaboration board with charcoal typography, pale ochre selection and peach attention badges. Flat solid warm neutral background #F8F2E7 across the whole sheet. Crisp dark charcoal #292720 lines, rounded caps and joins, optically uniform 2px-like stroke at a nominal 24px glyph size. Subtle 1960s technical-manual cartoon warmth through softly squared corners and modest friendly bot eyes. No faces on functional controls or state symbols. Clean digital vector-like edges, not a distressed print.

Composition: single large portrait contact sheet, target 2048 x 2560 pixels, three clearly separated sections with generous whitespace and small legible dark labels beneath each individual drawing. All drawings centered with comfortable cell gutters, no clipping or overlaps. No cell boxes, UI cards, shadows or decorative framing. Small heading "BOARD / FAMILY STUDY", section headings "CONTROLS", "TICKET STATES", "BOT IDENTITIES". Footer "REFERENCE ART / MANUAL VECTOR ADAPTATION". Keep every requested key present exactly once in its section. Do not create a giant hero mascot. Controls and states must remain highly readable and take priority over decoration.

CONTROLS: 35 monochrome outline glyphs in exactly five rows of seven, with these exact lowercase labels and silhouettes in this order:
row 1: "decisions" diamond containing an exclamation; "epics" rounded square with two short checklist lines; "seats" paired simple seat/person outlines; "library" archive box; "find" magnifying glass; "add" plus; "close" diagonal X.
row 2: "chevron" down chevron; "copy" two overlapping sheets; "external" arrow leaving an open square toward upper right; "back" left arrow; "forward" right arrow; "history" clock with a backward circular arrow; "files" folder.
row 3: "design" document with a folded corner; "work" small tray with a check; "reply" bent return arrow; "expand" two outward diagonal arrows; "collapse" two inward diagonal arrows; "attach" paperclip; "mention" @.
row 4: "help" circle with question mark; "send" paper plane; "preferences" simple gear; "usage" three ascending outlined bars; "refresh" two circular arrows; "filter" funnel; "sort" opposed vertical arrows.
row 5: "edit" pencil; "check" plain checkmark; "warning" triangle with exclamation; "more" three horizontal dots; "download" down arrow into tray; "link" two chain links; "play" right-facing triangle.
These are functional silhouettes, no incidental adornment. Stroke remains thin enough for calm UI use but strong enough at 16px.

TICKET STATES: exactly ten monochrome symbols in two rows of five; visibly different outer silhouettes and exact labels in this order:
row 1: "Drafted" paper plus pencil; "Designed" triangular set square with triangular cutout; "Signed off" scalloped seal with check; "Ready" flag on pole; "In progress" circular clock with clearly visible hands.
row 2: "In review" eye; "Blocked" octagon containing a horizontal bar; "Done" circle containing check; "Partial" circle with left half solid charcoal and right half empty; "Dropped" square containing diagonal X.
All states are distinguished by geometry without color. Keep Signed off scalloped seal distinct from Done circle. Keep In progress clock distinct from Partial half-filled circle. State glyphs are symbolic, no cartoon eyes except the literal eye symbol for In review.

BOT IDENTITIES: exactly eleven compact head/device illustrations in two rows, six then five. Related charcoal rounded outlines, minimal two-dot optical eyes, at most one small role motif integrated into each silhouette. Warm cream faceplate and at most one flat muted fill per bot, chosen sparingly from ochre #E9CD79, peach #E9AD98, teal #609C94, muted violet #8880B8. Identities must remain distinguishable in grayscale through head shape and role motif, not color. Front view, no bodies, no arms, no scene, no floating accessories. Make them readable at eventual 32px; small deliberate motifs rather than elaborate costumes. Exact lowercase labels:
row 1:
"owner" broad rounded-square bot with one simple key-shaped top antenna;
"coordinator" low rounded horizontal bot with three connected rounded nodes forming a top bridge;
"architect" roof-shaped triangular brow integrated into a squat square bot;
"engineer" hexagonal bot with a wrench-jaw notch integrated into its top contour;
"reviewer" round bot with one large single lens/monocle eye and one dot eye;
"adversary" angular shield-shaped bot with a split V brow, inquisitive and firm, never demonic or angry.
row 2:
"qa" rectangular bot whose upper-right outline incorporates a large check tab;
"sme" book-shaped bot with a central spine and two optical dots;
"consultant" speech-bubble-shaped bot face with a clear tail and two optical dots;
"system" stacked rounded device slabs with a simple central indicator, no face, not a person;
"unknown" simple dashed-outline rounded device tile with one question mark, no face, not a person.

Hard constraints: no human avatars or people portraits; existing humans are preserved elsewhere. No provider logos, no brand symbols, no flowers, gardens, leaves, clouds, stars, sparkles or scenery. No gradients, cloudy shading, texture, grain, drop shadows, glossy highlights, 3D or perspective. No oversized eyes, rubber-hose limbs, clothing or mascot bodies. No UI screenshot, navigation sidebar, conversation text, buttons or full app chrome. No presence-status row: presence is separate from ticket state. Labels are annotation only, never embedded in functional glyphs. All 56 requested drawings must fit fully within the sheet. Exact thin rounded line family and restrained functional clarity are more important than flourish.
